  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   Central Idea:\n   - Use Fourier basis to parametrize step functions with sparse coefficients (K=10 modes)\n   - Optimize coefficient magnitudes while maintaining function positivity\n   - Combine step-wise random restarts with filtering based on mean frequency content\n   \n   Why it could improve parent solution:\n   - Fourier parametrization globalizes the search space while reducing dimensionality\n   - Progressive resolution ensures proper exploration across scales\n   - Adaptive temperature allows balancing exploration and exploitation at different scales\n   \n   Bottleneck Addressed:\n   - Original grid-based search suffers from local optima due to high dimensionality\n   - Parametric representation enables capturing periodic structures naturally\n   - Fallback mechanism ensures solution robustness\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   - Representation & Variables:\n     * h(x) = A + \u2211_{k=1}^{K} [B_k cos(2\u03c0k x) + C_k sin(2\u03c0k x)]\n     * Coefficients {B_k, C_k} \u2208 \u211d (K=10)\n     * Temperature T configuration: [(\u03c4_i, iterations) for i=1..5]\n\n   - Objective:\n     * C_5 = (max_lag cross-correlation value) * (2/n_points)\n     * Minimize C_5 subject to constraints\n\n   - Constraints:\n     * Integral: \u222bh(x)dx = 1 \u2192 enforced via Lagrange multiplier\n     * Bounding: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2192 enforced via penalty terms\n\n   - Optimization Procedure:\n     * Use `scipy.optimize.minimize` with SLSQP method\n     * Temperature schedule: Start with low T for exploration\n     * Progressive resolution: 512 \u2192 1024 \u2192 2048\n     * Filter banks: Maintain archive of intervals with frequency content\n     * Seeds: Determine by Fourier transforms of base modes\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   - Initialization:\n     1. Check and validate parent input\n     2. Set initial temperature schedule T and max iterations\n     3. Sample n_points resolution (start=512)\n\n   - Core Algorithm:\n     1. Compute feasible solution from parent (upsampling)\n     2. Progressive resolution loop:\n        a. For T=1 to 5 levels:\n        b. Initialize from previous resolution\n        c. Multi-start with temperature schedule:\n            - Low K bases for broad exploration\n            - Medium K for exploitation\n            - High K for fine adjustment\n        d. Apply density-based filtering\n        e. Select best candidate based on C_5\n     3. Adjust resolution and continue\n\n   - Fallback:\n     1. Valid solution maintained via archives\n     2. Geometric restart from current best\n     3. Ensures progress even with failed filters\n\n4. Search Choices & Variations\n   - Default Parameters:\n     * K_max = 10 base Fourier frequencies\n     * T evolution: [(0.7, 300), (1.0, 300), (1.5, 300), (2.0, 300), (5.0, 300)]\n     * Max iterations: 1500\n     * Refinement steps: 3\n\n   - Key Adaptations:\n     * Linear scaling of base lags with resolution\n     * Thermal schedule adapts to remaining time budget\n     * Step size dynamically adjusts based on improvement\n\n   - Fitness Filter Variations:\n     * Memory-based top 10% of solutions preserved\n     * Biased toward increasing overall spectral power\n     * Adaptive exclusion for repetitive patterns\n\n5. Compute Budget & Robustness\n   - Time Estimation:\n     * Convex optimization cost: O(K*n_samples)*O(iterations)\n     * Approximate runtime: 800s across 3 resolution levels\n     * Monitoring: Time tracking within resolution loops\n\n   - Critical Safeguards:\n     * Time budget check implemented before expensive iterations\n     * Resolution ceiling at 2048 points\n     * Continuous feasibility update during optimization\n\n6. Validation & Return Contract\n   - Checks:\n     * Set(N_coeffs) matches initial specification\n     * Integral passed via top-level function validation\n     * Objective consistency ensured via repeated evaluation\n     * Latency-reduced overlap calculation using caching\n\n   - Return Format:\n     * (h_values, c5, n_points) where C5 = max_overlap * dx\n     * Type checks: h_values 1D array, float values between 0 and 1\n\n   - Sanity Checks:\n     * Test case: Half-rectified signal (should yield ~0.5)\n     * Early termination if C5 doesn't improve significantly",
